assistant: Subject: read unit_amount when price is missing in get_product
In vendor API version 2026-10-01, the product response sends the price as `unit_amount` instead of `price`, even though the published spec didn't change. `get_product` only read `p.price`, so `?? null` turned the missing field into a null price. The fix adds an optional `unit_amount` field to `VendorProduct` and maps the price as `p.price ?? p.unit_amount ?? null`. I assumed `unit_amount` uses the same unit as `price`: for p-1001 both versions return 1199, while v1 sent `price` and 2026-10-01 sent `unit_amount`. Older vendor responses still use `price` first, so the v1 fixtures give exactly the same output. Typecheck, lint and tests all pass, though no test covers the new 2026-10-01 response shape. `search_products` also reads `p.price` directly and may have the same problem under the new version; I didn't change it.

